# Bounded by design, not a leak to fix: each of the 30 workers traps inside a closure the runtime calls back from C, and those C frames have no landing pads on either backend (docs/effects-impl.md, "Frames of C code that a closure was called back from"). Native releases every kaikai frame through its pads and keeps nothing per trap. The C backend has no pads in kaikai frames either (docs/effects-impl.md, "The C backend has no pads") and keeps 5 per trap, 150 per run.
